        "original_id": "b82fee0e-714b-5150-b5f8-eb607996c4b3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Bowdoin College, Brown University, WBOR\n- Places: Maine, Massachusetts, Providence, Rhode Island, Brunswick, United States\n- Concepts: college charters, colonial colleges, Ivy League, research universities, radio stations\n\nFacts:\n- Bowdoin College was chartered in 1794, when Maine was still part of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts.\n- Brown University was founded in 1764 as the College in the English Colony of Rhode Island and Providence Plantations.\n- Brown University is the seventh-oldest institution of higher education in the United States and one of the nine colonial colleges chartered before the American Revolution.\n- Brown University is a private Ivy League research university in Providence, Rhode Island, United States.\n- WBOR is a radio station at 91.1 FM licensed to Bowdoin College in Brunswick, Maine, United States.",
